  "result_text": "**The median order value in June 2026 was $46.94**, across 349 orders. The mean was $54.23, so a few large orders pull it above the median.\n\n- **What I pulled:** one warehouse query per day for 2026-06-01 through 06-30, so 30 billed calls with no re-pulls. I assumed \"June\" means June 2026. The 06-01 call I used to check the output format was reused as that day's data.\n- **Coverage:** every day returned orders, between 9 and 15 per day, so no day is missing. On every day the stated order count matched the number of amounts listed. Amounts run from $8.27 to $184.10, with no negatives or zeros.\n- **What I couldn't check:** the tool returns only a count and a list of amounts, with no order IDs, status or currency fields. I therefore couldn't test for duplicate orders across days, or for cancelled or test orders. If those exist in the warehouse and should be excluded, the figure could shift. The middle values are tightly packed ($46.84, $46.87, $46.94, $47.10), so a few orders either way would move the median by only a few cents.\n\nThe collection plan and the raw per-day outputs (`day-2026-06-*.out`) are in `/var/folders/4_/s6fbcjyn4b13xdxkd3lv0kw00000gn/T/arm-s14-post-xzvuwvn4/work`."
